   "id": "9bce5732",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Teil 3: Mit Wetter-Datenbank verbinden und in pandas datetime object verwandeln"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d6d801c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Hier wird als nächstes die gleiche Logik wie bei den NextBike Daten angewandt. Eine Verbindung zur Wetterdatenbank wird über eine SQL-Query erstellt und die Daten werden anschließend ebenfalls in ein Stündliches Format gesetzt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "d0837521",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loading Weather-Data...\n",
      "Weather-Data successfully loaded!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Loading Weather-Data...\")\n",
    "conn_w = sqlite3.connect(\"Weather_Data_3.db\") \n",
    "\n",
    "weather_query = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT time, temp, prcp, wspd FROM karlsruhe_weather_09_2025\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT time, temp, prcp, wspd FROM karlsruhe_weather_10_2025\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "weather_df = pd.read_sql_query(weather_query, conn_w)\n",
    "weather_df['time'] = pd.to_datetime(weather_df['time'])\n",
    "weather_df['date'] = weather_df['time'].dt.date.astype(str)\n",
    "weather_df['hour'] = weather_df['time'].dt.hour.astype(int)\n",
    "weather_df['weekday'] = weather_df['time'].dt.weekday.astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Weather-Data successfully loaded!\")\n",
    "conn_w.close()"
   ]
  },
